<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Vertices of a feasible region</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>R is given by \({@D[1]@}\), \({@D[2]@}\), \(x \ge {@kx@}\) and \(y \ge 0\). Give exact values (fractions or decimals).</p><p>(a) Find the vertex where \({@D[3]@}\) meets \({@D[4]@}\): ( [[input:ans1]] , [[input:ans2]] ) [[validation:ans1]] [[validation:ans2]]</p><div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the vertex where \({@D[4]@}\) meets \(x = {@kx@}\): ( [[input:ans3]] , [[input:ans4]] ) [[validation:ans3]] [[validation:ans4]]</p><div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Two boundary lines meet at a vertex, so solve their equations together.</p><p>(a) Solve \({@D[3]@}\) and \({@D[4]@}\) together: eliminate one letter, then substitute back. The vertex is \({@V1d@}\).</p><p>(b) Put \(x = {@kx@}\) into \({@D[4]@}\): \({@a2@} \times {@kx@} + {@b2@}y = {@c2@}\), so \(y = {@v2y@}\). The vertex is \({@V2d@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
